==Sardinian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|sc|abblacare|abbracare||northern Logudorese}}

===Etymology===
Likely a borrowing. Compare {{cog|oc|abaucar||to calm; to calm down}}. The northern forms might be from a language of northern Italy (compare {{cog|lmo|balcà||to die down, calm down}}).<ref>{{R:sc:WagnerDES|ab(b)akkare}}</ref> Compare {{cog|sc-sro|abbacai}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sc|/abbaˈkare/}}

===Verb===
{{sc-verb}} {{lb|sc|Logudorese}}

# {{lb|sc|transitive}} to [[slow down]]
# {{lb|sc|transitive}} to [[calm down]] {{gl|to cause to become less excited, intense or angry}}
# {{lb|sc|intransitive}} to [[calm down]] {{gl|to become less intense}} {{q|of wind}}

